          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ઠાર (ṭhār) goes back to sthāra, \"firm, firmness\", a form CDIAL reconstructs; CDIAL lists the Gujarati word, \"frost\" (CDIAL 13765): the cold that makes things set hard."
            }
